<br><br>
Events are HTML code that activates Javascript code.
<br><br>
<input type="text" id="myText01" value="3">
<br><br>
<input
    type="button"
    value="Example onClick"
    onclick="
document.getElementById('myDiv01').innerHTML =
document.getElementById('myText01').value  "
>
<br><br>
<div id="myDiv01">...</div>
<br>
<b id="myB02"
   onmouseout="
       document.getElementById('myB02').innerHTML = 'This is nice.'
   "
   onmouseover="
       document.getElementById('myB02').innerHTML = 'This is cool.'
   ">
    This is bold
</b>
<br><br>
You do at least 8 other events:
<br>
onClick, onDBClick, onChange, onBlur, onFocus, onMouseMove,
onTouch, onKeyDown, onKeyPress, onDragStart, onTouchStart,
onTouchEnd, onTouchMove
</body>
</html>
